{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If it is your soul to bury my dead before me</b> — its meaning is: I will not bury my dead in another's grave, but if it is your desire that I bury my dead, intercede for me with Ephron, who has a cave at the edge of his field — and it is not their ancestral burial site, for to them it is a field. And the meaning of \"before me\" is that if you do not do so, I will bury him in a coffin. Or the meaning may be: my dead who is before me, and I must hasten to bury him. And the meaning of \"intercede for me\" is that Ephron was wealthy and honored, as he said, \"What is it between me and you?\" — and it would not be honorable for him to sell his ancestral inheritance, in the manner of Naboth the Jezreelite (see I Kings 21:6). Therefore Abraham did not go to him directly, so as not to drive up the price of the field, and he asked the men of the city to intercede on his behalf, out of respect."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:33.394801805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}